'' A WINDOWS int128 VARIADIC ARGUMENT IS PASSED BY ADDRESS ON BOTH WIDTHS. The
'' caller stores a 16-aligned copy and passes its pointer; the callee must read a
'' pointer-sized slot and load i128 through it. On i386 the old width guard read
'' a raw i128 slot instead, so caller and callee disagreed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win32 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/vararg-int128.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: va_arg ptr %
'' EXPECT-OUT: load i128, ptr %
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i128 (i32, ...) @"VSUM"(i32 2, ptr %
